Give the host embedding lookup the positions of an M-RoPE model
Fold-into: hexagon-host/0002-llama-host-timers-and-embd-lookup.patch

The defects. tests/fuzz/core/run.sh test replays the reproducer of each one.

- The host embedding lookup gives an M-RoPE model one position for each row.

  With LLAMA_EMBD_LOOKUP_HOST=1, llama_context::decode turns a token batch into an embedding
  batch. An M-RoPE model (Qwen3.5: n_pos_per_embd is 4) reads n_pos_per_embd positions for each
  row of an embedding batch, but the token batch has one position for each token. Thus
  llama_batch_allocr::ubatch_add reads past the end of the position array (an ASan report), and
  the model gets wrong positions and wrong logits.

  The change: embd_lookup gives the embedding batch n_pos_per_embd copies of the positions of the
  token batch, one copy for each section. A batch without a position array keeps its tokens.

  The reproducer: tests/fuzz/core/regress/fuzz_recurrent--embd-host-mrope.

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 with the patches of patches/series above this one.

Files:
    src/llama-context.cpp
    src/llama-context.h
--- a/src/llama-context.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-context.cpp
@@ -1484,6 +1484,21 @@ bool llama_context::embd_lookup(const llama_batch & batch) {
         return false;
     }
 
+    // An M-RoPE model (Qwen3.5: 4 positions for each row) reads n_pos_per_embd positions for
+    // each row of an embedding batch (the layout of an image), but a token batch has one
+    // position for each token. Give the embedding batch the positions of the token layout: one
+    // copy for each section. Without a position array the batch keeps its tokens.
+    const uint32_t n_pos = hparams.n_pos_per_embd();
+    if (n_pos > 1) {
+        if (!batch.pos) {
+            return false;
+        }
+        embd_lookup_pos.resize((size_t) batch.n_tokens * n_pos);
+        for (uint32_t j = 0; j < n_pos; j++) {
+            std::copy(batch.pos, batch.pos + batch.n_tokens, embd_lookup_pos.begin() + (size_t) j * batch.n_tokens);
+        }
+    }
+
     embd_lookup_buf.resize((size_t) batch.n_tokens * n_embd_inp);
 
     for (int32_t i = 0; i < batch.n_tokens; i++) {
@@ -1769,6 +1784,9 @@ int llama_context::decode(const llama_batch & batch_inp_user) {
     if (embd_lookup_host && embd_lookup(batch_inp_user)) {
         batch_inp.token = nullptr;
         batch_inp.embd  = embd_lookup_buf.data();
+        if (model.hparams.n_pos_per_embd() > 1) {
+            batch_inp.pos = embd_lookup_pos.data();
+        }
     }
 
     const auto & vocab   = model.vocab;
